00:32:55.680 --> 00:32:58.559
I would have moved the earth to make it there.
为了去那里，我移山填海都在所不惜。

00:32:58.559 --> 00:33:02.920
That night was single-handedly the best night of my life.
那天晚上是我一生中独一无二的最棒的夜晚。

00:33:02.920 --> 00:33:05.880
I brought my blue French horn and proudly displayed it.
我带上了我的蓝色法国号，并自豪地把它摆了出来。

00:33:05.880 --> 00:33:09.240
It sits signed on my mantle now.
现在它签了名，摆在我的壁炉架上。

00:33:09.240 --> 00:33:12.839
I've always been a hopeless romantic searching for my Ted Mosby.
我一直是一个无可救药的浪漫主义者，一直在寻找我的泰德·莫斯比（Ted Mosby）。

00:33:12.839 --> 00:33:18.119
At the benefit concert, I remember turning to my mom and saying, I wonder if I'll meet my Ted tonight?
在慈善音乐会上，我记得自己转头对妈妈说：“我不知道今晚会不会遇到我的泰德？”

00:33:18.119 --> 00:33:22.220
And much like Ted looking at Robin in the pilot, there he was.
就像泰德在试播集中看着罗宾那样，他就在那里。

00:33:22.220 --> 00:33:26.859
I could almost swear the background song from the pilot was playing in that moment.
我甚至敢发誓，那一刻试播集里的背景音乐正在响起。

00:33:26.859 --> 00:33:28.500
Maybe someone said, what's taking so long?
也许有人说：“怎么花了这么久？”

00:33:28.500 --> 00:33:29.500
No, I'm kidding.
不，开玩笑的。

00:33:29.500 --> 00:33:30.500
I added that part.
那句是我自己加的。

00:33:30.500 --> 00:33:31.500
Let's take it so long.
怎么花了这么久。

00:33:31.500 --> 00:33:36.960
We ended up talking for most of the concert, shared one of Victoria's cupcakes and exchange numbers.
我们最终在音乐会的大部分时间里都在聊天，分享了一个维多利亚的纸杯蛋糕，并交换了电话号码。

00:33:36.960 --> 00:33:39.259
We have been talking nonstop ever since.
从那以后，我们一直在不停地聊天。

00:33:39.259 --> 00:33:41.259
Oh my God, I love this.
噢天哪，我太喜欢这个了。

00:33:41.259 --> 00:33:42.799
He lives two mind blowing.
他住得太不可思议了。

00:33:42.799 --> 00:33:47.539
He lives 2,000 miles away, but I would walk 500 miles for him.
他住在两千英里之外，但我愿意为他走五百英里。

00:33:47.539 --> 00:33:48.539
In just a few weeks.
就在几周后。

00:33:48.539 --> 00:33:49.539
You've got to do that times four.
你得把那个乘以四。

00:33:49.539 --> 00:33:50.539
You've got to times that.
你得翻倍。

00:33:50.539 --> 00:33:51.539
You've got to multiply that.
你得乘以那个数。

00:33:51.539 --> 00:33:53.059
Well, they're getting to keep coming around.
好吧，他们还要继续见面。

00:33:53.059 --> 00:33:59.140
In just a few weeks, he is flying out to me and we are going on a four day super date.
就在几周后，他要坐飞机来看我，我们要进行为期四天的超级约会。

00:33:59.140 --> 00:34:04.019
I will be picking him up from the airport with a six pack of Utah brood beer.
我去机场接他时，会带上一六包犹他州的精酿啤酒。

00:34:04.019 --> 00:34:08.949
We both keep joking about how close we are to pulling a Ted Mosby.
我们俩一直开玩笑说，我们离上演“泰德·莫斯比式表白”有多近。

00:34:08.949 --> 00:34:09.949
What is a Ted Mosby?
什么是泰德·莫斯比式？

00:34:09.949 --> 00:34:12.469
Just like a, oh, oh, saying you love you.
就像是，哦，哦，说我爱你。

00:34:12.469 --> 00:34:14.789
I think I love you on the first date.
我觉得是在第一次约会上就说我爱你。

00:34:14.789 --> 00:34:15.789
Yeah.
对。

00:34:15.789 --> 00:34:21.010
felt so inclined to pull a Ted Mosby before, but he is absolutely perfect and brings it out of me.
以前从没想过要来个泰德·莫斯比式表白，但他实在是太完美了，把我内心的这一面激发了出来。

00:34:21.010 --> 00:34:26.610
If there's a wedding in the future, we're totally choosing a band, no DJ, people will dance.
如果以后有婚礼，我们绝对会选乐队，不要DJ，大家都要跳舞。

00:34:26.610 --> 00:34:27.610
Yes, Emily.
太对了，艾米莉。

00:34:27.610 --> 00:34:28.610
My favorite line.
我最喜欢的一句。

00:34:28.610 --> 00:34:29.610
Yes.
没错。

00:34:29.610 --> 00:34:38.730
Who knows if he's actually my Ted, but I know it will all be told as part of the epic details when I tell my kids the incredible story of how I met their father.
谁知道他是不是我真正的泰德呢，但我知道，当我把这不可思议的、我如何遇到他们父亲的故事讲给我的孩子们听时，这都将成为其中精彩细节的一部分。

00:34:38.730 --> 00:34:44.690
There are so many wonderful experiences and memories I have because of this show and the lessons it's taught me, and they keep on coming.
因为这部剧以及它教给我的道理，我有那么多美好的经历和回忆，而且它们还在继续。

00:34:44.690 --> 00:34:59.010
I really could go on all day about what a lovely story y'all have created and portrayed, but I will spare you the rest, keeping the amazing people you are, and thank you from the bottom of my heart for creating something so wonderful and meaningful, Emily from Utah.
真的，你们创作并呈现了一个如此美好的故事，我可以一整天都说个不停，但我还是不占用大家时间了，保持你们了不起的本色，从心底感谢你们创造了如此美妙而有意义的作品，来自犹他州的艾米莉。

00:34:59.010 --> 00:35:00.449
I can't handle this one.
我快招架不住这个了。

00:35:00.449 --> 00:35:02.050
I can't handle this one.
我简直没办法接受这个。

00:35:02.050 --> 00:35:04.710
Listen, Emily, we need a follow-up.
听着，艾米丽，我们需要后续。

00:35:04.710 --> 00:35:09.090
You have to let us know how the four-day date went.
你得让我们知道那四天的约会进展如何。

00:35:09.090 --> 00:35:14.090
We're now invested, and that's a lot of pressure, so just too much pressure.
我们现在已经深陷其中了，这压力太大了，真的是压力太大了。

00:35:14.090 --> 00:35:15.112
too much pressure.
压力太大了。

00:35:15.112 --> 00:35:18.690
But if you, if it goes well and you want to let us know, we'll.
但如果你，如果进展顺利，你想让我们知道，我们会……

00:35:18.690 --> 00:35:22.170
No, but her point is she's going to tell us either way, because it's all part of the story.
不，但她的意思是无论如何她都会告诉我们，因为这都是故事的一部分。

00:35:22.170 --> 00:35:24.909
Her point is whatever happens, it's all part of the story.
她的意思是无论发生什么，这都是故事的一部分。

00:35:24.909 --> 00:35:26.892
So we need to hear no matter what happens.
所以不管发生什么我们都得听听。

00:35:26.892 --> 00:35:27.931
Emily, that's amazing.
艾米丽，这太神奇了。

00:35:27.931 --> 00:35:29.537
I'm pretty sure we met that night.
我很确定我们那天晚上见过。

00:35:29.537 --> 00:35:31.851
I remember, I feel like I remember you from Utah.
我记得，我觉得我对你从犹他州来这事儿有印象。

00:35:31.851 --> 00:35:33.079
I remember being so moved.
我记得当时深受感动。

00:35:33.079 --> 00:35:35.818
That concert, like it was, you know, it was a bigger show.
那场音乐会，就像是，你知道的，是一场规模更大的演出。

00:35:35.818 --> 00:35:37.518
We then versions of like 300 people.
我们之前的版本大概只有300人左右。

00:35:37.518 --> 00:35:40.730
And now this was the Bowery, you can feel like 600-something people.
而现在这是包厘舞厅，感觉能容纳600多人。

00:35:40.730 --> 00:35:45.570
And people had come in from all over Mexico and England and Utah and all these different places.
人们从墨西哥、英国、犹他州以及所有这些不同的地方赶来。

00:35:45.570 --> 00:35:47.289
So moved the people did that.
大家能这么做，真的让人很感动。

00:35:47.289 --> 00:35:53.050
The idea that she came and maybe made this amazing connection, it's too good to be true.
她来了并且可能促成了一段美妙的姻缘，这种想法简直好得让人难以置信。

00:35:53.050 --> 00:35:59.889
I'm so honored that that happened, that she made the trip to support this cause and be there with us making music that night.
我很荣幸能发生这种事，她特地赶来支持这项事业，那天晚上和我们在一起创作音乐。

00:35:59.889 --> 00:36:02.690
And then I can't, I mean, we need the follow up.
然后我真的，我是说，我们需要后续。

00:36:02.690 --> 00:36:03.610
This is too good.
这太棒了。

00:36:03.610 --> 00:36:09.570
Good things happen to people who support Paul Gross Help Research, that is proven by this letter.
支持保罗·格罗斯帮助研究的人总会有好报，这封信就是证明。

00:36:09.570 --> 00:36:11.050
But thank you, Emily.
但谢谢你，艾米丽。

00:36:11.050 --> 00:36:14.010
Thank you so much, and we love hearing these.
非常感谢，我们很喜欢听这些故事。

00:36:14.010 --> 00:36:17.210
So keep them coming, and we'll see you next time.
所以请继续分享，我们下次见。

00:36:17.210 --> 00:36:19.590
I am guilty.
我有罪。

00:36:19.590 --> 00:36:21.510
Please equip me.
请赦免我。

00:36:21.510 --> 00:36:23.869
All sins are forgiven.
所有的罪孽都已被原谅。

00:36:23.869 --> 00:36:26.030
New York City.
纽约市。

